      "writtenOn": "2024-07-25T11:25:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, would\u0027ve been nice to know, before I updated all the signatures 😊. The logic in `onBehalfOf` in the Submit.java, does in fact already creates a user with \"realUser\" provided, it was just not used. Changed back to use a single user\n\nSide-note: I do find this way of using IdentifiedUser more error-prone, as it hard to know that this possibility exists, if you\u0027re not familiar and editing some code lower down the call-stack. But it does keep the signatures cleaner.",
      "parentUuid": "78a943aa_5fe46d15",
